{
  "_comment": [
    "Single source of truth for the Slang shader build, consumed by BOTH",
    "scripts/windows/Build-SlangShaders.ps1 and scripts/linux/compile-slang-shaders.sh.",
    "Keys starting with '_' are documentation only and ignored by the scripts.",
    "",
    "manifest: one row per (entry point, target). Add rows as shaders migrate.",
    "  file     : path relative to Resources/ShadersSlang (forward slashes)",
    "  entry    : entry-point function name",
    "  stage    : vertex | fragment | compute | miss | raygeneration | closesthit | ...",
    "  targets  : 'spirv' -> build/spirv/<subdir>/<base>.<entry>.spv (C++ Vulkan renderer)",
    "             'wgsl'  -> build/wgsl/<subdir>/<base>.<entry>.wgsl (Rust WebGPU renderer)",
    "  disabled : true keeps the row for documentation without compiling it",
    "",
    "wgslMap: combined WGSL emit — each source is compiled WITHOUT -entry/-stage",
    "  so ALL entry points land in one WGSL file, which is then copied into the",
    "  Rust crate's shader directory so include_str! picks up the Slang-emitted",
    "  WGSL (replaces hand-written WGSL).",
    "  src : Slang source relative to Resources/ShadersSlang",
    "  out : destination file name (also the depthTexturePatches key)",
    "  dst : destination directory relative to the repository root",
    "",
    "depthTexturePatches: per-output-file regex patches applied to the combined",
    "  WGSL before it is copied (see the _comment on that object). Patterns use",
    "  \\w / \\s classes, which both PowerShell -replace (.NET) and GNU sed -E",
    "  accept; replacements use ${N} group references (the bash script rewrites",
    "  ${N} to sed's \\N). Patterns must not contain '|' or '/' (sed delimiter",
    "  safety); replacements must not contain '&', '|' or '/'.",
    "",
    "minSlangcVersionForWgsl: lowest slangc version whose COMBINED (whole-module,",
    "  no -entry/-stage) WGSL emit is known to be correct. slangc",
    "  2026.1-52-gc8ddf20bb - the version shipped by Vulkan SDK 1.4.341.1, i.e.",
    "  the ANTfrastructure Linux image - drops the @location(N) attribute from every",
    "  non-builtin member of a varying struct in that mode (per-entry emits from",
    "  the SAME binary are correct), producing WGSL that wgpu/naga rejects. 2026.8",
    "  (Vulkan SDK 1.4.350.0) is correct and reproduces the checked-in files",
    "  byte-for-byte on BOTH Windows and Linux. Below the floor the compile",
    "  scripts SKIP the combined emit and leave the checked-in WGSL untouched;",
    "  at or above it they emit and then hard-fail on any varying struct member",
    "  that carries neither @builtin nor @location. See",
    "  docs/shader-build-pipeline.md."
  ],
  "minSlangcVersionForWgsl": "2026.8",
  "manifest": [
    { "_comment": "Rust/WebGPU tonemap pass (WGSL emit only).",
      "file": "tonemap/tonemap.slang", "entry": "vs_main", "stage": "vertex", "targets": ["wgsl"] },
    { "file": "tonemap/tonemap.slang", "entry": "fs_main", "stage": "fragment", "targets": ["wgsl"] },
    { "_comment": "C++/Vulkan post pass (SPIR-V emit only).",
      "file": "post/post.slang", "entry": "vs_main", "stage": "vertex", "targets": ["spirv"] },
    { "file": "post/post.slang", "entry": "fs_main", "stage": "fragment", "targets": ["spirv"] },
    { "_comment": "CI guard: verify the shared BRDF math emits to BOTH targets.",
      "file": "tests/brdf_test.slang", "entry": "brdf_test_main", "stage": "compute", "targets": ["spirv", "wgsl"] },
    { "_comment": "CI guard: verify the shared noise math emits to BOTH targets.",
      "file": "tests/noise_test.slang", "entry": "noise_test_main", "stage": "compute", "targets": ["spirv", "wgsl"] },
    { "_comment": "Vulkan ray tracing shaders (SPIR-V only — WebGPU has no RT pipeline).",
      "file": "raytracing/raytrace.rmiss.slang", "entry": "rmiss_main", "stage": "miss", "targets": ["spirv"] },
    { "file": "raytracing/shadow.rmiss.slang", "entry": "shadow_rmiss_main", "stage": "miss", "targets": ["spirv"] },
    { "file": "raytracing/raytrace.rgen.slang", "entry": "rgen_main", "stage": "raygeneration", "targets": ["spirv"] },
    { "file": "raytracing/raytrace.rchit.slang", "entry": "rchit_main", "stage": "closesthit", "targets": ["spirv"] },
    { "file": "raytracing/raytrace.rahit.slang", "entry": "rahit_main", "stage": "anyhit", "targets": ["spirv"] },
    { "_comment": "Path tracing compute kernel (ray query, SPIR-V only).",
      "file": "path_tracing/path_tracing.slang", "entry": "path_tracing_main", "stage": "compute", "targets": ["spirv"] },
    { "_comment": "Skybox (cubemap, SPIR-V only).",
      "file": "skybox/skybox.slang", "entry": "vs_main", "stage": "vertex", "targets": ["spirv"] },
    { "file": "skybox/skybox.slang", "entry": "fs_main", "stage": "fragment", "targets": ["spirv"] },
    { "_comment": "Compute noise volume (SPIR-V only).",
      "file": "compute/noise.slang", "entry": "noise_main", "stage": "compute", "targets": ["spirv"] },
    { "_comment": "Compute clouds (volumetric, SPIR-V only).",
      "file": "compute/clouds.slang", "entry": "clouds_main", "stage": "compute", "targets": ["spirv"] },
    { "_comment": "Forward rasterizer (SPIR-V only).",
      "file": "rasterizer/rasterizer.slang", "entry": "vs_main", "stage": "vertex", "targets": ["spirv"] },
    { "file": "rasterizer/rasterizer.slang", "entry": "fs_main", "stage": "fragment", "targets": ["spirv"] },
    { "_comment": "Deferred geometry + lighting (SPIR-V only).",
      "file": "deferred/deferred.slang", "entry": "geometry_vs_main", "stage": "vertex", "targets": ["spirv"] },
    { "file": "deferred/deferred.slang", "entry": "geometry_fs_main", "stage": "fragment", "targets": ["spirv"] },
    { "file": "deferred/deferred.slang", "entry": "lighting_vs_main", "stage": "vertex", "targets": ["spirv"] },
    { "file": "deferred/deferred.slang", "entry": "lighting_fs_main", "stage": "fragment", "targets": ["spirv"] },
    { "_comment": "Cascaded shadow map (SPIR-V only).",
      "file": "rasterizer/shadows/shadow_map.slang", "entry": "shadow_vs_main", "stage": "vertex", "targets": ["spirv"] },
    { "file": "rasterizer/shadows/shadow_map.slang", "entry": "shadow_fs_main", "stage": "fragment", "targets": ["spirv"] },
    { "_comment": "Rust/WebGPU forward PBR pass (WGSL emit).",
      "file": "forward/forward.slang", "entry": "vs_main", "stage": "vertex", "targets": ["wgsl"] },
    { "file": "forward/forward.slang", "entry": "fs_main", "stage": "fragment", "targets": ["wgsl"] },
    { "file": "forward/forward.slang", "entry": "vs_shadow", "stage": "vertex", "targets": ["wgsl"] },
    { "file": "forward/forward.slang", "entry": "vs_shadow_masked", "stage": "vertex", "targets": ["wgsl"] },
    { "file": "forward/forward.slang", "entry": "fs_shadow_masked", "stage": "fragment", "targets": ["wgsl"] },
    { "_comment": "Rust/WebGPU procedural sky (WGSL emit).",
      "file": "sky/sky.slang", "entry": "vs_main", "stage": "vertex", "targets": ["wgsl"] },
    { "file": "sky/sky.slang", "entry": "fs_main", "stage": "fragment", "targets": ["wgsl"] },
    { "_comment": "Rust/WebGPU bloom (WGSL emit).",
      "file": "bloom/bloom.slang", "entry": "vs_main", "stage": "vertex", "targets": ["wgsl"] },
    { "file": "bloom/bloom.slang", "entry": "fs_brightpass", "stage": "fragment", "targets": ["wgsl"] },
    { "file": "bloom/bloom.slang", "entry": "fs_blur_h", "stage": "fragment", "targets": ["wgsl"] },
    { "file": "bloom/bloom.slang", "entry": "fs_blur_v", "stage": "fragment", "targets": ["wgsl"] },
    { "_comment": "Rust/WebGPU SSAO (WGSL emit).",
      "file": "ssao/ssao.slang", "entry": "vs_main", "stage": "vertex", "targets": ["wgsl"] },
    { "file": "ssao/ssao.slang", "entry": "fs_ssao", "stage": "fragment", "targets": ["wgsl"] },
    { "file": "ssao/ssao.slang", "entry": "fs_blur", "stage": "fragment", "targets": ["wgsl"] },
    { "_comment": "Rust/WebGPU IBL precompute (WGSL emit).",
      "file": "ibl/ibl.slang", "entry": "vs_fullscreen", "stage": "vertex", "targets": ["wgsl"] },
    { "file": "ibl/ibl.slang", "entry": "fs_equirect_to_cube", "stage": "fragment", "targets": ["wgsl"] },
    { "file": "ibl/ibl.slang", "entry": "fs_downsample_cube", "stage": "fragment", "targets": ["wgsl"] },
    { "file": "ibl/ibl.slang", "entry": "fs_irradiance", "stage": "fragment", "targets": ["wgsl"] },
    { "file": "ibl/ibl.slang", "entry": "fs_prefilter", "stage": "fragment", "targets": ["wgsl"] },
    { "file": "ibl/ibl.slang", "entry": "fs_brdf_lut", "stage": "fragment", "targets": ["wgsl"] },
    { "_comment": "Rust/WebGPU GPU occlusion culling (WGSL emit).",
      "file": "gpu_cull/gpu_cull.slang", "entry": "cs_main", "stage": "compute", "targets": ["wgsl"] },
    { "_comment": "Rust/WebGPU occlusion bbox detection (WGSL emit).",
      "file": "occlusion_bbox/occlusion_bbox.slang", "entry": "vs_main", "stage": "vertex", "targets": ["wgsl"] },
    { "file": "occlusion_bbox/occlusion_bbox.slang", "entry": "fs_main", "stage": "fragment", "targets": ["wgsl"] },
    { "_comment": "Rust/WebGPU depth resolve (WGSL emit).",
      "file": "depth_resolve/depth_resolve.slang", "entry": "vs_main", "stage": "vertex", "targets": ["wgsl"] },
    { "file": "depth_resolve/depth_resolve.slang", "entry": "fs_main", "stage": "fragment", "targets": ["wgsl"] },
    { "_comment": "Rust/WebGPU GUI tex quad (WGSL emit).",
      "file": "tex_quad/tex_quad.slang", "entry": "vs_main", "stage": "vertex", "targets": ["wgsl"] },
    { "file": "tex_quad/tex_quad.slang", "entry": "fs_main", "stage": "fragment", "targets": ["wgsl"] }
  ],
  "wgslMap": [
    { "src": "forward/forward.slang", "out": "forward.wgsl", "dst": "third_party/OxidANT/crates/webgpu_renderer/src/shaders" },
    { "src": "sky/sky.slang", "out": "sky.wgsl", "dst": "third_party/OxidANT/crates/webgpu_renderer/src/shaders" },
    { "src": "bloom/bloom.slang", "out": "bloom.wgsl", "dst": "third_party/OxidANT/crates/webgpu_renderer/src/shaders" },
    { "src": "ssao/ssao.slang", "out": "ssao.wgsl", "dst": "third_party/OxidANT/crates/webgpu_renderer/src/shaders" },
    { "src": "ibl/ibl.slang", "out": "ibl.wgsl", "dst": "third_party/OxidANT/crates/webgpu_renderer/src/shaders" },
    { "src": "gpu_cull/gpu_cull.slang", "out": "gpu_cull.wgsl", "dst": "third_party/OxidANT/crates/webgpu_renderer/src/shaders" },
    { "src": "tonemap/tonemap.slang", "out": "tonemap.wgsl", "dst": "third_party/OxidANT/crates/webgpu_renderer/src/shaders" },
    { "src": "depth_resolve/depth_resolve.slang", "out": "depth_resolve.wgsl", "dst": "third_party/OxidANT/crates/webgpu_renderer/src/shaders" },
    { "src": "occlusion_bbox/occlusion_bbox.slang", "out": "occlusion_bbox.wgsl", "dst": "third_party/OxidANT/crates/webgpu_renderer/src/shaders" },
    { "src": "tex_quad/tex_quad.slang", "out": "tex_quad.wgsl", "dst": "third_party/OxidANT/crates/gui/src/shaders" }
  ],
  "depthTexturePatches": {
    "_comment": [
      "Slang's WGSL backend has no depth-texture resource type in HLSL syntax",
      "(a Texture2DArray/Texture2DMS<float> sampled via SampleCmp/Load from a",
      "depth-format image), so it always emits the sampled-float WGSL type even",
      "where the Rust bind group layout declares TextureSampleType::Depth.",
      "Patch the emitted declaration(s) until slangc gains a depth-texture",
      "control (checked 2026-07-31: no such control exists yet)."
    ],
    "forward.wgsl": [
      { "pattern": "(var shadowMap_\\w+\\s*:\\s*)texture_2d_array<f32>", "replacement": "${1}texture_depth_2d_array" }
    ],
    "depth_resolve.wgsl": [
      { "pattern": "(var msaaDepth_\\w+\\s*:\\s*)texture_multisampled_2d<f32>", "replacement": "${1}texture_depth_multisampled_2d" },
      { "_comment": [
          "textureLoad on texture_multisampled_2d<f32> returns vec4<f32> (hence",
          "Slang's trailing .x); textureLoad on texture_depth_multisampled_2d",
          "returns f32 directly, so the accessor becomes invalid once the type",
          "above is patched. Drop it from this specific call."
        ],
        "pattern": "(textureLoad\\(\\(msaaDepth_\\w+\\), \\(\\w+\\), \\(i32\\(\\w+\\)\\)\\))\\.x", "replacement": "${1}" },
      { "_comment": [
          "`fs_main` writes the depth aspect itself (SV_Depth in the Slang",
          "source), not a colour target - the Rust pipeline declares zero",
          "colour attachments for this pass. Slang's WGSL backend still emits",
          "a plain `@location(0)` output struct member, so it is silently",
          "dropped and the rasterizer's own fragment z (0.0, since the",
          "fullscreen triangle's NDC z is hard-coded to 0.0) gets written",
          "instead. Retarget the output at the depth builtin. Safe for this",
          "file: the only other `@location(0)` is `uv_0 : vec2<f32>`, excluded",
          "by the `: f32,` anchor."
        ],
        "pattern": "@location\\(0\\) (\\w+) : f32,", "replacement": "@builtin(frag_depth) ${1} : f32," }
    ],
    "ssao.wgsl": [
      { "pattern": "(var depthTex_\\w+\\s*:\\s*)texture_2d<f32>", "replacement": "${1}texture_depth_2d" },
      { "_comment": [
          "See the depth_resolve.wgsl comment above: textureLoad on",
          "texture_depth_2d returns f32 directly, so the trailing .x Slang",
          "emitted for the texture_2d<f32> case becomes invalid."
        ],
        "pattern": "(textureLoad\\(\\(depthTex_\\w+\\), \\(\\(\\w+\\)\\)\\.xy, \\(\\(\\w+\\)\\)\\.z\\))\\.x", "replacement": "${1}" }
    ],
    "gpu_cull.wgsl": [
      { "pattern": "(var depthTex_\\w+\\s*:\\s*)texture_2d<f32>", "replacement": "${1}texture_depth_2d" },
      { "pattern": "(textureLoad\\(\\(depthTex_\\w+\\), \\(\\(\\w+\\)\\)\\.xy, \\(\\(\\w+\\)\\)\\.z\\))\\.x", "replacement": "${1}" }
    ]
  }
}
